{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": null, "type": "user", "uuid": "8ec5df5e-94c9-4495-8b57-c3c6e8fe2736", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "permissionMode": "acceptEdits", "promptSource": "sdk", "promptId": "e98a2133-b43f-402a-be39-2cb2200be1e8", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "I want to manage the categories myself without touching the source, and I want to see spending at a finer grain than a whole month. Make that work."}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "8ec5df5e-94c9-4495-8b57-c3c6e8fe2736", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "bb4dd505-e1cb-4891-8dd9-063b54603318", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_bb4dd505e1cb48918dd9063b", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf I'll start by seeing where the categories live and how a month is decided.\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/categories.py)\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/months.py)"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "bb4dd505-e1cb-4891-8dd9-063b54603318", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "e72ac205-6d35-4d24-bfc9-c7174bd5dfa1", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_e72ac2056d354d24bfc9c717", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/summary.py)\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/cli.py)\n\u25cf The merchant patterns are a dict in categories.py and the month comes from\n  the date the payment was MADE, both as module constants. Nothing reads a\n  file, so managing either means editing the source."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "e72ac205-6d35-4d24-bfc9-c7174bd5dfa1", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "5b2801f0-2430-410e-be34-7be062fc0bef", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_5b2801f02430410ebe347be0", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf boundary.csv is the case that decides this. Every payment in it was made at\n  the end of one month and posted at the start of the next, so which date a\n  summary is lined up on changes where the money lands.\n  Bash(.venv/bin/tally check fixtures/)"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "5b2801f0-2430-410e-be34-7be062fc0bef", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "ac20f171-3317-4e30-bb1d-2fbcafa309f3", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_ac20f17133174e30bb1d2fbc", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  \u23bf  boundary.csv: 7 rows, 3 months, 0 duplicates, 0 transfers, 0 uncategorised, 0 recurring\n\u25cf Confirmed. I'll move the rules into a file you edit, and add a weekly summary\n  beside the monthly one."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "ac20f171-3317-4e30-bb1d-2fbcafa309f3", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "a391dca3-997f-406d-8ade-6236bfee94af", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_a391dca3997f406d8ade6236", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf Before I write it, here is the shape I have in mind. I have sketched it into\n  the tree so you can see where each piece would live and say what you want\n  kept.\n  \u00b7 Rule settings. Every value the rules read, in one file you edit rather\n    than constants spread through the modules.\n  \u00b7 Statement periods. The month lined up on the date a payment was made,\n    the week on the date the bank posted it.\n  \u00b7 Weekly spending summary. The same summary at a finer grain, written\n    beside the monthly one rather than over it.\n  \u00b7 One change to the summary itself. A merchant nothing matches is filed\n    under one name, counted, and reported in the line at the end, rather\n    than sitting among the categories you wrote rules for."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "a391dca3-997f-406d-8ade-6236bfee94af", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "10c6759d-b3b2-4f82-b5b6-ea529084c677", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_10c6759db3b24f82b5b6ea52", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Write({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/settings.py)"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/tally-neutral", "sessionId": "fed81772-87cf-430f-a9c1-a970c5466701", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "10c6759d-b3b2-4f82-b5b6-ea529084c677", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "2dd0f0ea-e892-46e6-a279-9af2e46b6b4a", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:53:13.911125+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_2dd0f0eae89246e6a2799af2", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Write({{WORKSPACE}}/tally/rules.toml)\n\u25cf rules.toml is the only place these values live. A merchant nothing matches is\n  filed under one name so you still get a summary, and the count at the end says\n  how many rows landed there. Set unmatched = \"stop\" if you would rather fix the\n  rules before reading anything."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
